    "author_association": "COLLABORATOR",
    "body": "## Bug\n\nShell terminal tabs created inside a session on the macOS direct-PTY preview remain open when the tab close button or Command-W is used. Their PTY processes also remain alive. Rename requests use the same broken route parameter.\n\n**Source:** User report in AO session on 2026-08-27  \n**Reported by:** preview tester  \n**Preview:** `0.12.0-pr4473.202608270716`  \n**Analyzed against:** `4c05344f831e9951ae69457af01e3433a9819164`  \n**Priority:** medium \u2014 shell tabs and PTYs cannot be closed through the UI, but typing `exit` is a workaround  \n**Confidence:** high\n\n## Reproduction\n\n1. On macOS, run the direct-PTY feature preview from PR #4473.\n2. Open an auxiliary shell terminal inside an agent session.\n3. Click the X on its terminal tab or press Command-W.\n4. Observe that the tab remains and the PTY host is still registered.\n\nThe generated frontend client reproduces the failure directly: DELETE returns 404 `SHELL_TERMINAL_NOT_FOUND` for `ptyhost-v1%3Ashellterm-...`, while GET still returns the unescaped `ptyhost-v1:shellterm-...` row.\n\n## Root Cause\n\n`runtimeselect` prefixes new macOS direct handles with `ptyhost-v1:`. `openapi-fetch` correctly percent-encodes the colon when substituting `{handleId}` in `/api/v1/shell-terminals/{handleId}`. `backend/internal/httpd/controllers/shell_terminals.go` passes `chi.URLParam(r, \"handleId\")` to the service without path-unescaping it, so storage looks for the literal `%3A` form and returns not found.\n\nLegacy tmux handles contain no colon, which is why the pre-direct-host path worked.\n\n## Fix\n\nPath-unescape the shell-terminal handle at the HTTP controller boundary for DELETE and PATCH, reject malformed escapes, and cover encoded direct-host handles in controller tests. Keep persisted runtime handles unchanged for backward compatibility.\n\n## Impact\n\n- Close button and Command-W silently fail for new macOS direct-host shell terminals.\n- Rename also fails for the same handles.\n- Failed closes leak the PTY until the user types `exit`, ends the owning session, or restarts AO.\n\n## Related\n\n- PR #4473 \u2014 macOS direct PTY host rollout.",
